{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nThe task asks me to implement a `solve(case)` function that allocates a budget across segments to maximize importance-weighted allocation, subject to minimum and capacity constraints.\n\nLet me analyze the problem:\n- Each segment has a `name`, `importance`, `minimum`, and `capacity`\n- We have a total `budget` to allocate\n- Each segment must get at least `minimum` units\n- Each segment can get at most `capacity` units\n- We want to maximize total importance (greedy: allocate to highest importance first after minimums)\n\nThe output should be:\n- `allocations`: array of integers (one per segment, in order)\n- `by_name`: dict mapping segment name to allocation\n- `total`: sum of all allocations\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. First, give each segment its minimum allocation\n2. Compute remaining budget\n3. Greedily allocate remaining budget to segments by importance (highest first), up to their capacity\n\nLet me verify with the first fixture:\n- Segments: s0(imp=8, min=1, cap=6), s1(imp=5, min=1, cap=5), s2(imp=1, min=1, cap=5), s3(imp=9, min=1, cap=5)\n- Budget: 11\n- Start: allocate minimums: [1,1,1,1] = 4 used, 7 remaining\n- Sort by importance desc: s3(9), s0(8), s1(5), s2(1)\n- s3: can get up to 5-1=4 more, allocate 4 → remaining: 3, s3 allocation: 5\n- s0: can get up to 6-1=5 more, allocate 3 → remaining: 0, s0 allocation: 4\n- Result: [4,1,1,5], total=11\n- by_name: {s0:4, s1:1, s2:1, s3:5}\n\nLet me verify case 001:\n- Segments: s0(imp=3, min=1, cap=6), s1(imp=2, min=1, cap=3), s2(imp=6, min=1, cap=6), s3(imp=4, min=1, cap=4)\n- Budget: 12\n- Minimums: [1,1,1,1]=4, remaining=8\n- Sort by imp desc: s2(6), s3(4), s0(3), s1(2)\n- s2: can get up to 6-1=5 more, allocate 5 → remaining=3, s2=6\n- s3: can get up to 4-1=3 more, allocate 3 → remaining=0, s3=4\n- Result: [1,1,6,4], total=12\n- by_name: {s0:1, s1:1, s2:6, s3:4}\n\nCase 002:\n- Segments: s0(imp=1, min=1, cap=3), s1(imp=5, min=1, cap=4), s2(imp=5, min=1, cap=5), s3(imp=4, min=1, cap=4)\n- Budget: 11\n- Minimums: [1,1,1,1]=4, remaining=7\n- Sort by imp desc: s1(5, idx=1), s2(5, idx=2), s3(4, idx=3), s0(1, idx=0)\n  - Tie-breaking: for equal importance, I need a consistent rule. Let me use the original index (lower index first for ties, or maybe importance desc then index asc)\n- s1: can get up to 4-1=3 more, allocate 3 → remaining=4, s1=4\n- s2: can get up to 5-1=4 more, allocate 4 → remaining=0, s2=5\n- Result: [1,4,5,1], total=11\n- by_name: {s0:1, s1:4, s2:5, s3:1}\n\nThis seems reasonable. Let me write the implementation.\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    segments = case[\"segments\"]\n    budget = case[\"budget\"]\n    n = len(segments)\n    \n    # Start with minimum allocations\n    allocations = [seg[\"minimum\"] for seg in segments]\n    remaining = budget - sum(allocations)\n    \n    # Sort by importance descending (stable sort preserves original order for ties)\n    order = sorted(range(n), key=lambda i: -segments[i][\"importance\"])\n    \n    for i in order:\n        if remaining \u003c= 0:\n            break\n        seg = segments[i]\n        can_add = seg[\"capacity\"] - allocations[i]\n        add = min(can_add, remaining)\n        if add \u003e 0:\n            allocations[i] += add\n            remaining -= add\n    \n    total = sum(allocations)\n    by_name = {seg[\"name\"]: allocations[i] for i, seg in enumerate(segments)}\n    \n    return {\n        \"allocations\": allocations,\n        \"by_name\": by_name,\n        \"total\": total\n    }\n```\n\nThis looks correct. Now I need to format this as a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing the Python source as a JSON string.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    segments = case[\\\"segments\\\"]\\n    budget = case[\\\"budget\\\"]\\n    n = len(segments)\\n\\n    # Start with minimum allocations\\n    allocations = [seg[\\\"minimum\\\"] for seg in segments]\\n    remaining = budget - sum(allocations)\\n\\n    # Sort indices by importance descending; stable sort preserves original order for ties\\n    order = sorted(range(n), key=lambda i: -segments[i][\\\"importance\\\"])\\n\\n    for i in order:\\n        if remaining \u003c= 0:\\n            break\\n        seg = segments[i]\\n        can_add = seg[\\\"capacity\\\"] - allocations[i]\\n        add = min(can_add, remaining)\\n        if add \u003e 0:\\n            allocations[i] += add\\n            remaining -= add\\n\\n    total = sum(allocations)\\n    by_name = {seg[\\\"name\\\"]: allocations[idx] for idx, seg in enumerate(segments)}\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"allocations\\\": allocations,\\n        \\\"by_name\\\": by_name,\\n        \\\"total\\\": total\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_0108N7AJVj2G5gYsMGZAAF00","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1466},"cache_creation_input_tokens":1466,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":58,"output_tokens":1589,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1314},"service_tier":"standard"}}